                  <provenance>The volume was written for a tertiary of the Dominican order (fols 124v-125v and fol. 146v)</provenance>
                  
                  <provenance>St Torpetus or Torpes of Pisa has an entry in the Calendar on 30th April</provenance>
                  
                  <provenance>With the arms of Adorno of Genoa</provenance>
                  
                  <provenance>In the litany (fol. 131v): 'Oremus pro papa nostro Sixto' (Sixtus IV, 1471-1484)</provenance>
                  
                  <provenance>Liturgical evidence for Piedmont: 'Frater Philippus de Arpo (? Muro)' is written in the large initial <hi rend="bold">S</hi> 
                     on <ref target="https://digital.bodleian.ox.ac.uk/objects/50c2175d-0c7c-4148-8bab-4db954a5ab3f/surfaces/75c42b76-b05d-400c-a1d5-8bb2a0d2290e/">fol. 150r</ref>
                  </provenance>
                  
                  <provenance><persName key="person_2384880" role="fmo">Matteo Luigi Canonici (1727– <hi rend="italic">c</hi>. 1806)</persName></provenance>
                  <provenance notAfter="1807" resp="#SC">Following Canonici's death, the collection passed to his brother, <persName key="person_446" role="fmo">Giuseppe Canonici</persName>, and 
